on/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-95a842f7-3cad-55fe-864e-f9f95a189d31" :answer-field/id #uuid "95a842f7-3cad-55fe-864e-f9f95a189d31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-febc1aab-e4e2-516a-89a4-59e4cc665b7c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7191899b-a4fc-5077-a73d-777a40c78957" "answer-febc1aab-e4e2-516a-89a4-59e4cc665b7c" "answer-0cfd3dd0-a244-5f4e-b880-23a88295a405" "answer-de47de1f-699e-5e9c-afe6-e4b6f5884354" "answer-988bbee4-95b2-561d-bf45-066ee3822370"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7191899b-a4fc-5077-a73d-777a40c78957" :answer/id #uuid "7191899b-a4fc-5077-a73d-777a40c78957" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Full or Straight" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-febc1aab-e4e2-516a-89a4-59e4cc665b7c" :answer/id #uuid "febc1aab-e4e2-516a-89a4-59e4cc665b7c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Null or Full" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0cfd3dd0-a244-5f4e-b880-23a88295a405" :answer/id #uuid "0cfd3dd0-a244-5f4e-b880-23a88295a405" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Other" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de47de1f-699e-5e9c-afe6-e4b6f5884354" :answer/id #uuid "de47de1f-699e-5e9c-afe6-e4b6f5884354" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Right" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-988bbee4-95b2-561d-bf45-066ee3822370" :answer/id #uuid "988bbee4-95b2-561d-bf45-066ee3822370" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Straight" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-043b7624-13fa-54e2-8595-1777662d58cb" :question/id #uuid "043b7624-13fa-54e2-8595-1777662d58cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-114728" :question/problem "![](images/8d/8db6c94bb486e77be9c5b281a8bc551c6c3811319e6fb8a0f8488fbd7eab6b4f.png)\n\nWhat type of angle is $∠SOT,$ shown in the figure above?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the vertex of $∠SOT$ is point $O,$ not point $T.$ So $∠SOT$ is *not* a straight angle.\n\nWe can think of $∠SOT$ as:\n\n- a *null* angle, if we assume that it doesn't turn at all (diagram on the left), or\n\n- a *full* angle, if we assume that it makes one full turn (diagram on the right).\n\n![](images/bd/bd3002843b8a0542d17604da7360d60a180e87b6a4f2c1f9e26476ad761a49f7.png)\n\nSo, the answer is 'Null' or 'Full'." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3654fa0c-ddf9-52e3-b3c7-95e98eb0283e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3654fa0c-ddf9-52e3-b3c7-95e98eb0283e" :answer-field/id #uuid "3654fa0c-ddf9-52e3-b3c7-95e98eb0283e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-165e88c9-93a8-5e51-9f92-a2c215d71808" :answer-field/choices ["answer-00626d6e-47ea-5b73-ace3-c239ab797dda" "answer-165e88c9-93a8-5e51-9f92-a2c215d71808" "answer-6b7e7b12-9f4d-5261-b76d-4ecbfb81a241" "answer-769926c3-11ee-58c2-acb5-fe893758aadf" "answer-f5beb084-beb9-511d-b08b-053c3b4519df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00626d6e-47ea-5b73-ace3-c239ab797dda" :answer/id #uuid "00626d6e-47ea-5b73-ace3-c239ab797dda" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Full or Straight" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-165e88c9-93a8-5e51-9f92-a2c215d71808" :answer/id #uuid "165e88c9-93a8-5e51-9f92-a2c215d71808" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Null or Full" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b7e7b12-9f4d-5261-b76d-4ecbfb81a241" :answer/id #uuid "6b7e7b12-9f4d-5261-b76d-4ecbfb81a241" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Other" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-769926c3-11ee-58c2-acb5-fe893758aadf" :answer/id #uuid "769926c3-11ee-58c2-acb5-fe893758aadf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Right" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5beb084-beb9-511d-b08b-053c3b4519df" :answer/id #uuid "f5beb084-beb9-511d-b08b-053c3b4519df" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Straight" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186111837 :tutorial/content "Some angles have special names.\n\n- A **right angle** has a measure of $90^\\circ.$ It corresponds to one-quarter of a full turn.\n\n![](images/15/155a1d6d2abd868b05674dec47ef4b20a5147d30cd328a5ba53d00dea271d65c.png)\n\n- A **straight angle**, which is just a straight line, has a measure of $180^\\circ.$ It corresponds to one-half of a full turn.\n\n![](images/24/2423950f80de8354aee74c4f1daa6e42cf376caa0365307c76ebc7e09f96c8cf.png)\n\n- A **null angle** has a measure of $0^\\circ.$ You can imagine \"closing\" the angle until the two sides of the angle overlap. In this case, we don't have any turn, so its measure is zero!\n\n![](images/f8/f86b7c1b7ba758fb6b07b6aeabd03395d29103b45e4cd220444b675f70a6e630.png)\n\n- A **full angle** has a measure of $360^\\circ.$ You can imagine \"opening\" the angle until one of the sides goes all the way around. So, this is the angle between a ray and itself after it has made one full turn.\n\n![](images/cb/cbc9e288f4d3905357539a221954328ef0ac799531fab62f034364d32a7c0f29.png)\n\nOn a diagram, null and full angles can look the same, so it is up to us what we choose to call it." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110864 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
